# Files that must not ship in the plugin ZIP.
#
# The release workflow reads this. It used to rely on .gitattributes
# export-ignore, which only applies to `git archive` -- the workflow builds
# with rsync, so export-ignore did nothing at all and every file below was
# going out in the release.

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.distignore

# Tooling and editor state
bin
.editorconfig
.vscode
.idea
phpcs.xml
phpcs.xml.dist
phpunit.xml
phpunit.xml.dist
composer.json
composer.lock
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules
vendor/bin

# Development documentation. readme.txt is what the directory reads, and
# every .md file in here is for the repository instead: README.md duplicates
# readme.txt, and the rest are working notes and defect reports that quote
# real order numbers and support addresses. The wildcard is the point -- the
# named entries below kept working while anything new quietly shipped.
*.md
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md

# Tests
tests
.phpunit.result.cache
